I'm the founder of Crypto Bot: a calm autopilot for Bitcoin,

3
00:00:04,884 --> 00:00:07,199
Ethereum and Solana that trades on

4
00:00:07,249 --> 00:00:10,400
Solana and can record every decision on-chain.

5
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:13,031
I'm a senior software engineer

6
00:00:13,081 --> 00:00:15,163
with ten years in web development.

7
00:00:15,213 --> 00:00:18,111
In March, I built seven day-trading strategies.

8
00:00:18,161 --> 00:00:21,810
Backtested on Binance history, none had an edge after fees.

9
00:00:21,860 --> 00:00:25,009
Bots like that overtrade, can't prove their record,

10
00:00:25,059 --> 00:00:26,200
and hold your keys.

11
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,092
So I built the opposite: one slow decision a day.

12
00:00:30,142 --> 00:00:32,144
Price above its moving averages?

13
00:00:32,194 --> 00:00:34,324
Hold more of the coin. Below them?

14
00:00:34,374 --> 00:00:35,350
Wait in dollars.

15
00:00:36,150 --> 00:00:39,053
After the daily close, the bot computes the signal,

16
00:00:39,103 --> 00:00:40,211
plans the rebalance,

17
00:00:40,261 --> 00:00:43,800
and swaps through Jupiter straight from the user's own wallet.

18
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:46,932
Each decision can be written to Solana

19
00:00:46,982 --> 00:00:49,376
with the Memo program before any order.

20
00:00:49,426 --> 00:00:52,760
Block time can't be backdated, so anyone can check it.

21
00:00:52,810 --> 00:00:53,700
Devnet for now.

22
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:58,040
Backtested on Bitcoin and Ethereum since twenty eighteen,

23
00:00:58,090 --> 00:01:00,307
with fees: forty-two percent a year,

24
00:01:00,357 --> 00:01:02,637
versus twenty-three for buy and hold,

25
00:01:02,687 --> 00:01:04,338
at about half the drawdown.

26
00:01:04,388 --> 00:01:05,975
A backtest, not a promise.

27
00:01:06,775 --> 00:01:08,359
Solana makes it practical:

28
00:01:08,409 --> 00:01:10,748
Jupiter quoted about four cents to buy

29
00:01:10,798 --> 00:01:13,324
and sell five hundred dollars of Bitcoin,

30
00:01:13,374 --> 00:01:15,650
versus about a dollar on an exchange.

31
00:01:16,450 --> 00:01:19,047
Starting takes a click and a confirmation.

32
00:01:19,097 --> 00:01:22,576
The app explains every trade in plain words, in English,

33
00:01:22,626 --> 00:01:23,900
Russian and Armenian.

34
00:01:24,700 --> 00:01:25,878
It's non-custodial,

35
00:01:25,928 --> 00:01:29,173
